  "id": "Compound::DB00786 - Gene::4320",
  "verbalization": "Marimastat is likely to interact with Matrix Metalloproteinases (MMPs) through binding to specific MMPs such as Mmp23b, Mmp27, or Mmp26, which are all members of the MMP family. These MMPs are known to play a role in the regulation of extracellular matrix remodeling and are involved in various physiological and pathological processes. The fact that all three MMPs are classified as \"participated by\" Mmp11 suggests a potential functional relationship between Marimastat and Mmp11, possibly through the modulation of MMP activity. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a strong, reliable interaction, though the exact mechanism of how Marimastat influences Mmp11 remains to be elucidated. The shared involvement of MMPs in the pathway implies that Marimastat may act as a regulator of MMP expression or activity, potentially affecting Mmp11 through a broader network of MMP-mediated processes.",
